# NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 (30 controls)
nist-800-53 AC-2 | Access Control | Account Management | caps data-change,detect-change | nist AC-2
nist-800-53 AC-6(9) | Access Control | Least Privilege | Log Use of Privileged Functions | caps data-auth,data-process,detect-privilege | nist AC-6(9)
nist-800-53 AC-7 | Access Control | Unsuccessful Logon Attempts | caps data-auth,detect-auth | nist AC-7 | also The limit and the lockout are set on each system. Signalith shows the failed sign-ins and detects attacks on accounts.
nist-800-53 AU-2 | Audit and Accountability | Event Logging | caps data-auth,data-process,data-change | nist AU-2
nist-800-53 AU-3 | Audit and Accountability | Content of Audit Records | caps record-content | nist AU-3
nist-800-53 AU-4 | Audit and Accountability | Audit Log Storage Capacity | caps storage-guard | nist AU-4
nist-800-53 AU-5 | Audit and Accountability | Response to Audit Logging Process Failures | caps source-health,notify | nist AU-5
nist-800-53 AU-6 | Audit and Accountability | Audit Record Review, Analysis, and Reporting | caps detect-any,triage | nist AU-6
nist-800-53 AU-7 | Audit and Accountability | Audit Record Reduction and Report Generation | caps search | nist AU-7
nist-800-53 AU-8 | Audit and Accountability | Time Stamps | caps timestamps,config-checks | nist AU-8
nist-800-53 AU-9 | Audit and Accountability | Protection of Audit Information | caps siem-access,siem-tls,siem-secrets | nist AU-9 | also Events cannot be changed from Signalith, but OpenSearch does not make them immutable; whoever can write to it directly can.
nist-800-53 AU-11 | Audit and Accountability | Audit Record Retention | caps retention-1y | nist AU-11
nist-800-53 AU-12 | Audit and Accountability | Audit Record Generation | caps data-any,config-checks | nist AU-12
nist-800-53 CA-7 | Assessment, Authorization, and Monitoring | Continuous Monitoring | caps detect-any,config-checks,vuln-scan | nist CA-7,CM-6
nist-800-53 CM-6 | Configuration Management | Configuration Settings | caps config-checks | nist CM-6
nist-800-53 CM-7 | Configuration Management | Least Functionality | caps config-checks | nist CM-7
nist-800-53 CM-8 | Configuration Management | System Component Inventory | caps assets,data-inventory | nist CM-8
nist-800-53 IA-5 | Identification and Authentication | Authenticator Management | caps config-checks | nist IA-5
nist-800-53 IR-4 | Incident Response | Incident Handling | caps cases,response,detect-any | nist IR-4
nist-800-53 IR-5 | Incident Response | Incident Monitoring | caps cases,triage | nist IR-5
nist-800-53 IR-6 | Incident Response | Incident Reporting | caps notify | nist IR-6 | also Reporting an incident to the people and authorities who must know is yours to do; Signalith sends the alerts that start it.
nist-800-53 PM-16 | Program Management | Threat Awareness Program | caps intel | nist PM-16
nist-800-53 RA-5 | Risk Assessment | Vulnerability Monitoring and Scanning | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5
nist-800-53 SC-8 | System and Communications Protection | Transmission Confidentiality and Integrity | caps config-checks | nist SC-8
nist-800-53 SC-28 | System and Communications Protection | Protection of Information at Rest | caps config-checks | nist SC-28
nist-800-53 SI-2 | System and Information Integrity | Flaw Remediation | caps vuln-scan,config-checks | nist SI-2
nist-800-53 SI-3 | System and Information Integrity | Malicious Code Protection | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
nist-800-53 SI-4 | System and Information Integrity | System Monitoring | caps detect-any,data-process,data-network,notify | nist SI-4
nist-800-53 SI-5 | System and Information Integrity | Security Alerts, Advisories, and Directives | caps intel | nist SI-5
nist-800-53 SI-7 | System and Information Integrity | Software, Firmware, and Information Integrity | caps data-files | nist SI-7
# CIS Controls v8 (20 controls)
cis-v8 1.1 | Inventory of Enterprise Assets | Keep a detailed inventory of enterprise assets | caps assets,data-inventory | nist CM-8
cis-v8 2.1 | Inventory of Software Assets | Keep an inventory of installed software | caps data-inventory | nist CM-8
cis-v8 4.1 | Secure Configuration | Keep a secure configuration process | caps config-checks | nist CM-6,CM-7 | also The safeguard asks for a documented configuration process; Signalith's checks show how hosts are configured.
cis-v8 7.1 | Continuous Vulnerability Management | Run a vulnerability management process | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5 | also The safeguard asks for a documented vulnerability management process; Signalith's scans are part of it.
cis-v8 7.5 | Continuous Vulnerability Management | Scan internal assets for vulnerabilities automatically | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5
cis-v8 8.2 | Audit Log Management | Collect audit logs | caps data-auth,data-process,data-change | nist AU-2,AU-12
cis-v8 8.3 | Audit Log Management | Keep enough storage for audit logs | caps storage-guard | nist AU-4
cis-v8 8.4 | Audit Log Management | Use consistent time across systems | caps timestamps,config-checks | nist AU-8
cis-v8 8.5 | Audit Log Management | Collect detailed audit logs | caps record-content,data-process | nist AU-3
cis-v8 8.6 | Audit Log Management | Collect DNS query logs | caps data-dns | nist 
cis-v8 8.8 | Audit Log Management | Collect command-line logs | caps data-process | nist 
cis-v8 8.9 | Audit Log Management | Keep audit logs in one central place | caps data-any | nist 
cis-v8 8.10 | Audit Log Management | Keep audit logs for at least 90 days | caps retention-90 | nist AU-11
cis-v8 8.11 | Audit Log Management | Review audit logs regularly | caps detect-any,triage | nist AU-6
cis-v8 10.1 | Malware Defenses | Run anti-malware software | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
cis-v8 13.1 | Network Monitoring and Defense | Centralize security event alerting | caps detect-any,notify | nist SI-4
cis-v8 13.2 | Network Monitoring and Defense | Detect intrusions on hosts | caps data-process,detect-any | nist SI-4
cis-v8 13.3 | Network Monitoring and Defense | Detect intrusions on the network | caps data-network,detect-network | nist SI-4
cis-v8 13.6 | Network Monitoring and Defense | Collect network traffic flow logs | caps data-network | nist 
cis-v8 17.4 | Incident Response Management | Run an incident response process | caps cases,response | nist IR-4 | also The written process, roles and exercises are yours; Signalith records the investigations that follow it.
# PCI DSS v4.0.1 (26 controls)
pci-dss 2.2.1 | 2: Secure configurations | Configuration standards are applied to system components | caps config-checks | nist CM-6,CM-7
pci-dss 5.2.1 | 5: Malware protection | Anti-malware runs on all in-scope system components | caps data-malware | nist SI-3 | also Every in-scope system must run anti-malware. Signalith counts antivirus events, not hosts, so check each system reports.
pci-dss 5.2.2 | 5: Malware protection | Anti-malware detects and handles known malware | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
pci-dss 5.3.4 | 5: Malware protection | Anti-malware logs are kept | caps data-malware,retention-1y | nist 
pci-dss 6.3.1 | 6: Secure systems and software | Security vulnerabilities are found and ranked | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5
pci-dss 6.3.3 | 6: Secure systems and software | Security patches are installed | caps vuln-scan,config-checks | nist SI-2
pci-dss 10.2.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Audit logs are on for all system components | caps data-any,data-auth,data-process | nist AU-2,AU-12 | also Every in-scope system must log. Signalith counts events by kind, not by host, so check each system sends.
pci-dss 10.2.1.2 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Actions by administrators are logged | caps data-auth,data-process,detect-privilege | nist AC-6(9)
pci-dss 10.2.1.4 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Failed access attempts are logged | caps data-auth,detect-auth | nist 
pci-dss 10.2.1.5 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Changes to accounts and credentials are logged | caps data-change,detect-change | nist AC-2
pci-dss 10.2.2 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Log records hold the required details | caps record-content | nist AU-3
pci-dss 10.3.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Read access to audit logs is limited | caps siem-access | nist AU-9
pci-dss 10.3.2 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Audit logs are protected from change | caps siem-access,siem-tls | nist AU-9 | also Events cannot be changed from Signalith, but OpenSearch does not make them immutable; whoever can write to it directly can.
pci-dss 10.3.3 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Audit logs are copied promptly to a central log server | caps data-any | nist 
pci-dss 10.4.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Security events are reviewed at least daily | caps detect-any,triage | nist AU-6 | also Signalith shows findings are reviewed within 7 days; reviewing every day is a process you run.
pci-dss 10.4.1.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Log reviews are automated | caps detect-any | nist 
pci-dss 10.4.3 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Exceptions and anomalies are followed up | caps triage,cases | nist IR-5
pci-dss 10.5.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Logs are kept 12 months, with 3 months at hand | caps retention-90,retention-1y | nist AU-11
pci-dss 10.6.1 | 10: Logging and monitoring | System clocks use synchronized time | caps timestamps,config-checks | nist AU-8
pci-dss 10.7.2 | 10: Logging and monitoring | Failures of security controls are detected and alerted | caps source-health,notify | nist AU-5
pci-dss 11.3.1 | 11: Testing security | Internal vulnerability scans run at least every three months | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5
pci-dss 11.5.1 | 11: Testing security | Intrusions are detected and alerted | caps detect-any,detect-network,notify | nist SI-4
pci-dss 11.5.2 | 11: Testing security | Changes to critical files are detected | caps data-files | nist SI-7
pci-dss 12.5.1 | 12: Policies and programs | An inventory of in-scope system components is kept | caps assets,data-inventory | nist CM-8
pci-dss 12.10.1 | 12: Policies and programs | An incident response plan is ready to use | caps cases,response | nist IR-4 | also The written plan, roles and tests are yours; Signalith records the investigations and responses that follow it.
pci-dss 12.10.5 | 12: Policies and programs | The response plan covers alerts from security monitoring | caps notify,triage,data-files | nist IR-6 | also The response plan itself is a document you keep; Signalith provides the alerts it covers.
# ISO/IEC 27001 2022 (13 controls)
iso-27001 A.5.7 | Organizational controls | Gather and use threat intelligence | caps intel | nist PM-16
iso-27001 A.5.9 | Organizational controls | Keep an inventory of assets | caps assets,data-inventory | nist CM-8
iso-27001 A.5.24 | Organizational controls | Plan and prepare for incidents | caps cases,response | nist IR-4 | also Planning, roles and procedures are yours; Signalith records the investigations that follow them.
iso-27001 A.5.25 | Organizational controls | Assess security events | caps triage | nist IR-5
iso-27001 A.5.26 | Organizational controls | Respond to incidents | caps cases,response | nist IR-4
iso-27001 A.5.28 | Organizational controls | Collect and keep evidence | caps cases,retention-1y | nist 
iso-27001 A.8.2 | Technological controls | Privileged access rights are managed | caps data-auth,detect-privilege | nist AC-6(9) | also Granting and restricting privileged access is done in your directory and systems; Signalith watches how it is used.
iso-27001 A.8.7 | Technological controls | Protect against malware | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
iso-27001 A.8.8 | Technological controls | Manage technical vulnerabilities | caps vuln-scan | nist RA-5,SI-2
iso-27001 A.8.9 | Technological controls | Manage secure configurations | caps config-checks | nist CM-6
iso-27001 A.8.15 | Technological controls | Produce, keep and protect logs | caps data-any,retention-1y,siem-access | nist AU-2,AU-12 | also Events cannot be changed from Signalith, but OpenSearch does not make them immutable; whoever can write to it directly can.
iso-27001 A.8.16 | Technological controls | Monitor for unusual behaviour | caps detect-any,data-network,notify | nist SI-4
iso-27001 A.8.17 | Technological controls | Synchronize clocks | caps timestamps,config-checks | nist AU-8
# HIPAA Security Rule 45 CFR 164 Subpart C (7 controls)
hipaa 164.308(a)(1)(ii)(D) | Administrative safeguards | Information system activity review | caps detect-any,triage | nist AU-6
hipaa 164.308(a)(5)(ii)(B) | Administrative safeguards | Protection from malicious software | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
hipaa 164.308(a)(5)(ii)(C) | Administrative safeguards | Log-in monitoring | caps data-auth,detect-auth | nist AC-7
hipaa 164.308(a)(6)(ii) | Administrative safeguards | Response and reporting | caps cases,notify,response | nist IR-4
hipaa 164.312(b) | Technical safeguards | Audit controls | caps data-any,data-auth,data-process | nist AU-2,AU-12
hipaa 164.312(c)(1) | Technical safeguards | Integrity | caps data-files | nist SI-7
hipaa 164.312(e)(1) | Technical safeguards | Transmission security | caps config-checks | nist SC-8
# SOC 2 TSC 2017 (rev. 2022) (5 controls)
soc2 CC6.8 | Logical and physical access | Unauthorized or malicious software is prevented or detected | caps data-malware,detect-malware | nist SI-3
soc2 CC7.1 | System operations | Configuration changes and vulnerabilities are detected | caps config-checks,vuln-scan,data-files | nist CM-6
soc2 CC7.2 | System operations | System components are monitored for anomalies | caps data-any,detect-any,notify | nist SI-4
soc2 CC7.3 | System operations | Security events are evaluated | caps triage,cases | nist IR-5
soc2 CC7.4 | System operations | Security incidents are responded to | caps cases,response | nist IR-4
# NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555 (14 controls)
nis2 21(2)(a) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Risk analysis and information system security | caps vuln-scan,config-checks | nist RA-5,CM-6 | also The policies are yours; Signalith supplies scan and configuration results for them.
nis2 21(2)(b) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Incident handling | caps detect-any,triage,cases,response | nist IR-4,IR-5
nis2 21(2)(e) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Vulnerability handling in maintaining systems | caps vuln-scan,config-checks | nist RA-5,SI-2
nis2 21(2)(f) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Assess whether the security measures work | caps config-checks,vuln-scan,detect-any | nist CA-7,CM-6 | also NIS2 asks for policies and procedures to assess the measures; Signalith's checks and scans are evidence for them.
nis2 21(2)(g) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Basic cyber hygiene | caps config-checks,data-malware,detect-malware | nist CM-6,SI-3 | also Basic cyber hygiene includes training, which Signalith cannot show.
nis2 21(2)(h) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Cryptography and encryption | caps config-checks,siem-tls | nist SC-8,SC-28 | also NIS2 asks for policies on the use of cryptography; Signalith checks encryption settings on hosts and its own connections.
nis2 21(2)(i) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Access control and asset management | caps assets,data-inventory,data-change,detect-change | nist AC-2,CM-8 | also This also covers human resources security and access control policies, which Signalith cannot show.
nis2 21(2)(j) | Art. 21: Risk-management measures | Multi-factor authentication | caps siem-mfa,data-auth,detect-auth | nist IA-2 | also NIS2 asks for multi-factor authentication across your systems, not only for Signalith; Signalith shows its own setting and watches sign-ins.
nis2 23(1) | Art. 23: Reporting obligations | Significant incidents are found and reported without undue delay | caps detect-any,notify,triage | nist IR-6,SI-4 | also Notifying the CSIRT or competent authority is yours to do; Signalith helps you find the incident in time.
nis2 23(4)(a) | Art. 23: Reporting obligations | Early warning within 24 hours | caps notify,triage,cases | nist IR-6 | also Sending the early warning to your CSIRT or authority is yours; Signalith helps you notice in time and keeps the record.
nis2 23(4)(b) | Art. 23: Reporting obligations | Incident notification within 72 hours, with severity, impact and indicators | caps cases,record-content,intel | nist IR-6 | also Writing and sending the notification is yours; the investigation holds what goes into it.
nis2 23(4)(d) | Art. 23: Reporting obligations | Final report within one month, with root cause and measures taken | caps cases,search,retention-90 | nist IR-4 | also Writing and sending the final report is yours; the investigation holds what goes into it.
nis2 IR 3.2 | Implementing Regulation 2024/2690 (digital providers) | Monitoring and logging | caps data-any,data-auth,data-network,detect-any,timestamps,siem-access,retention-90 | nist AU-2,AU-6,AU-12,SI-4
nis2 IR 3.5 | Implementing Regulation 2024/2690 (digital providers) | Incident response | caps cases,response,notify | nist IR-4
# GDPR (EU) 2016/679 (11 controls)
gdpr 5(1)(e) | Personal data in your logs | Logs are kept no longer than needed | caps retention-limit | nist 
gdpr 5(1)(f) | Personal data in your logs | Logs are protected from unauthorized access and change | caps siem-access,siem-tls,siem-secrets | nist  | also Events cannot be changed from Signalith, but OpenSearch does not make them immutable; whoever can write to it directly can.
gdpr 5(2) | Personal data in your logs | Who did what in Signalith is recorded | caps siem-audit,siem-access | nist 
gdpr 25 | Personal data in your logs | Data protection by default in the SIEM | caps siem-access,siem-mfa,retention-limit | nist 
gdpr 32(1)(a) | Art. 32: Security of processing | Encryption of personal data | caps config-checks,siem-tls | nist SC-8,SC-28
gdpr 32(1)(b) | Art. 32: Security of processing | Ongoing confidentiality, integrity and availability | caps data-auth,detect-any,source-health,storage-guard | nist SI-4,AU-5
gdpr 32(1)(d) | Art. 32: Security of processing | Security measures are tested and assessed regularly | caps config-checks,vuln-scan | nist CA-7,CM-6,RA-5 | also Article 32 asks for a process covering organisational measures too; Signalith shows the technical checks.
gdpr 33(1) | Art. 33-34: Personal data breaches | Breaches are noticed in time to notify within 72 hours | caps detect-any,detect-network,notify,triage | nist IR-6,SI-4 | also Deciding whether a breach must be notified, and notifying the supervisory authority, are yours.
gdpr 33(3) | Art. 33-34: Personal data breaches | The notification can describe the breach and its likely consequences | caps cases,search,record-content | nist IR-4 | also Writing the notification is yours; the investigation and searches hold what goes into it.
gdpr 33(5) | Art. 33-34: Personal data breaches | Every breach is documented, with its facts, effects and remedial action | caps cases,retention-1y | nist IR-5
gdpr 34 | Art. 33-34: Personal data breaches | The people affected can be found and told | caps cases,search,assets | nist IR-6 | also Telling the people affected is yours; searches and asset lists help find who they are.
